      "title": "(review)",
      "headword": "(review)",
      "romanization": "(review)",
      "gloss": "three places and one question — said aloud, because a grid of twelve forms is not what you reach for when somebody is waiting for an answer",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:689798517b4fb580",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three words, three places, in order. (Este, ese, aquel.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three chants. Say each one, then say who it belongs to."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First. Este libro — by me. The word Latin used to point at you, walked one step closer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second. Ese libro — by you. The word that used to mean self, moved in when the first one left."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third. Aquel libro — by neither. The word that also became el, kept stressed and propped up so it could go on pointing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: one question, asked twice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Everything else here is two questions, in this order."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do I have a noun? If no, use the -o form and stop: esto, eso, aquello. Nothing to agree with, so nothing agrees."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "If yes — whose side is it on? Then pick from the three, agree it with the noun, and put it in front, in the article's place. Never el este libro; the pointing word already did the article's job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the three chants, in order, without looking",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the three chants, in order, without looking]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "¿Qué es esto?, then answer it and point again with a noun",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *¿Qué es esto?*, then answer it and point again with a noun]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C59-repaso-demostrativos-side",
              "prompt": "A book is an arm's length away, right next to the person you are speaking to. Este or ese?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-DEMONSTRATIVE-ESE"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 13,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "ese",
                "ese, it is on their side"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Sides, not metres.",
                "incorrect": "Ese -- it is on their side, however close it is to you."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C59-repaso-demostrativos-noun",
              "prompt": "Which question do you ask first, before choosing a form?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-DEMONSTRATIVE-NEUTER"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 14,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "do i have a noun",
                "whether there is a noun at all"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "No noun, no agreement -- take the -o form.",
                "incorrect": "Whether you have a noun at all."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C59-repaso-demostrativos-article",
              "prompt": "What does the pointing word push out of the sentence?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-DEMONSTRATIVE-BEFORE-NOUN"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 12,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "the article",
                "el, la -- the article"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "One word per job.",
                "incorrect": "The article. Never el este libro."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two origins worth keeping. What did ese mean in Latin? (Self.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And which everyday word is aquel related to? (El — both from ille, one worn down, one propped up.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": []
}
